{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>In plowing time and in harvest time you shall rest.</b> According to the plain sense, Scripture mentions plowing and harvest because in them lies the essence of human sustenance. And it mentions the Sabbath in the midst of the festivals, because it placed it adjacent to the Festival of Matzot and to the sanctification of the firstborn, because all of them are a remembrance of the work of Creation, for in the Exodus from Egypt there is a sign and wonder in it, as I explained in the Decalogue (Ramban on Exodus 20:2). And further, because Scripture says that the Sabbath too is a remembrance of the Exodus from Egypt, as it says in the latter Decalogue (Deuteronomy 5:15): \"And you shall remember that you were a servant in the land of Egypt, and YHWH your Elohim brought you out from there; therefore YHWH your Elohim commanded you to keep the Sabbath day.\" And there I will explain, with the help of the blessed Name, may He be exalted:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The closing formula ובעזרת הש\"י ויתרומם is rendered as 'with the help of the blessed Name, may He be exalted'; הש\"י is an abbreviation for השם יתברך, here rendered 'the blessed Name' per the divine-name conventions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:31.614443220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}